definitions.layout_body:
A request to the runtime infrastructure (RTI) for the kinds of data (class attributes as well as interactions) that the joined federate is currently interested in receiving. The RTI uses these data along with publication data received from other joined federates to support services, such as:
\begin{hladefinitionlist}
\item \HLAService{Start/Stop Registration}
\item \HLAService{Turn On/Off Updates}
\item \HLAService{Turn On/Off Interactions}
\end{hladefinitionlist}
The RTI also uses the subscription (and publication) data to determine how to route data to the joined federates that require that data.

\begin{hladefinitionlist}
\item Pertaining to an object class: the dimensions associated with that object class in union with the set of inherited dimensions in the federation object model (FOM).
\item Pertaining to an attribute: The available dimensions of an instance attribute are the available dimensions of the known class. When registering, subscribing, unsubscribing, requesting updates with regions, or getting available dimensions, the available dimensions are the available dimensions of the object class specified in the service invocation.
\item Pertaining to an interaction class: the dimensions associated with that interaction class in union with the set of inherited dimensions in the FOM. The available dimensions of a sent interaction are the available dimensions of the interaction class specified in the \HLAService{Send Interaction With Regions} service invocation.
\end{hladefinitionlist}
\HLADefinitionNote{See 9.1 in IEEE Std 1516.1\HLAStandardMark-2025.}
\par\addvspace{9.96pt}See dimension.

\begin{hladefinitionlistroomy}[36.00pt]
\item {\addfontfeatures{FakeStretch=1.000}Pertaining to an object class from the perspective of a given joined federate: having subscribed attributes of that class or subscribed attributes of that class with regions, for some region. \HLASeeAlso{\HLATermReference{subscribed attributes of an object class}\HLASemicolon{} \HLATermReference{subscribed attributes of an object class with regions}.}}
\item Pertaining to an interaction class: being a subscribed interaction class or a subscribed interaction class with regions, for some region. \HLASeeAlso{\HLATermReference{subscribed interaction class}\HLASemicolon{} \HLATermReference{subscribed interaction class with regions}.}
\end{hladefinitionlistroomy}

The interval between a joined federate's request to advance its time position and the corresponding grant by the runtime infrastructure (RTI). A joined federate may advance its time position only by requesting a time advancement from the RTI via one of the following services:
\begin{hladefinitionservicelist}
\item \HLAService{Time Advance Request}
\item \HLAService{Time Advance Request Available}
\item \HLAService{Next Message Request}
\item \HLAService{Next Message Request Available}
\item \HLAService{Flush Queue Request}
\end{hladefinitionservicelist}
\par\vspace*{5.02pt}
The joined federate's time position will not actually be advanced until the RTI responds with a \HLAService{Time Advance Grant} \HLAPrintersDagger{} or \HLAService{Flush Queue Grant} \HLAPrintersDagger{} service invocation at that joined federate.

\begin{hladefinitionlistdisplay}
\item Pertaining to a region and the specified interaction class designator: being an argument in the \HLAService{Send Interaction With Regions} service.
\item Pertaining to the default region: when the specified interaction class designator is an argument in the \HLAService{Send Interaction} service.
\HLADefinitionListNote[12.04pt]{See 9.1 of IEEE Std 1516.1\HLAStandardMark-2025.}
\end{hladefinitionlistdisplay}

\vspace*{1.05pt}
\begin{hladefinitionlistdisplay}
\item Pertaining to a region, an object class, and a class attribute: when the class attribute is a subscribed attribute of the object class with that region. See also: subscribed attributes of an object class with regions.
\HLADefinitionListNote[9.85pt]{See 9.1 of IEEE Std 1516.1\HLAStandardMark-2025.}
\vspace*{3.84pt}
\item Pertaining to the default region: when the specified class attribute is a subscribed attribute of the specified class. See also: subscribed attributes of an object class with regions.
\HLADefinitionListNote[11.58pt]{See 9.1 of IEEE Std 1516.1\HLAStandardMark-2025.}
\end{hladefinitionlistdisplay}

\vspace*{-1.02pt}
\begin{hladefinitionlistdisplay}
\item Pertaining to a region and an interaction class: when the interaction class is a subscribed interaction class with regions. \HLASeeAlso{\HLATermReference{subscribed interaction class}.}
\HLADefinitionListNote[11.78pt]{See 9.1 of IEEE Std 1516.1\HLAStandardMark-2025.}
\vspace*{5.88pt}
\item Pertaining to the default region: when the specified interaction class is a subscribed interaction class. \HLASeeAlso{\HLATermReference{subscribed interaction class}.}
\HLADefinitionListNote[11.84pt]{See 9.1 of IEEE Std 1516.1\HLAStandardMark-2025.}
\end{hladefinitionlistdisplay}

\vspace*{0.18pt}
\begin{hladefinitionlistdisplaytightbottom}
\item Pertaining to a region that, along with the specified object instance and attribute designators, has been used as an argument in either the \HLAService{Register Object Instance With Regions} service or the \HLAService{Associate Regions For Updates} service: when the region has not subsequently been used along with the specified object instance designator as an argument in the \HLAService{Unassociate Regions For Updates} service, nor has the joined federate subsequently lost ownership of the specified instance attribute(s).
\HLADefinitionListNote[9.78pt]{See 9.1 of IEEE Std 1516.1\HLAStandardMark-2025.}
\vspace*{3.90pt}
\item Pertaining to the default region: when the specified instance attribute(s) is not currently used for update with any other region.
\HLADefinitionListNote[7.80pt]{See 9.1 of IEEE Std 1516.1\HLAStandardMark-2025.}
\end{hladefinitionlistdisplaytightbottom}
